---
title: Your account
description: Two-factor authentication, hiding amounts, language, usage and more.
---

Everything about your account is in the menu with your name, at the bottom of the sidebar.

## Two-factor authentication

Your account holds your accounting, so give it a second lock. With two-factor authentication, signing in asks for a code from an authenticator app on top of your password.

{% steps %}

1. Open the menu with your name and go to your account settings.

2. Under **Two-factor authentication**, choose **Turn on** and confirm your password.

3. Scan the QR code with your authenticator app. If you can't scan it, enter the text code instead.

4. Enter the 6-digit code shown in your app.

5. Copy your **backup codes** and keep them somewhere safe. Each one lets you sign in once if you lose your phone. They won't be shown again.

{% /steps %}

From now on, nullish asks for a code after your password. You can tick **Trust this device** to skip the code on that device for 30 days.

{% aside type="tip" %}
Lost your authenticator app? Choose **Use a backup code** when signing in. Once you're back in,
generate new backup codes from your account settings, the old ones stop working.
{% /aside %}

## Hide amounts

Working in a café, or sharing your screen? Choose **Hide amounts** in the menu. Every amount in the app is blurred until you choose **Show amounts** again.

## Language

nullish speaks English, German, French and Italian. Switch under **Language** in the menu.

## Password

Change your password from your account settings. Your other devices are signed out right away.

## Usage

The **Usage** tab shows how much you've used the assistant this month, per model. If you hit the assistant's limit, wait a bit and try again.

## Delete your account

Leaving us? First leave or delete your organizations, and delete your [API keys](/en/assistant/#connect-your-own-ai-agent). Then choose **Delete my account** in your account settings and confirm with your password.
